      ":question/id": "b8c6e450-fe10-5923-accc-8b824e3c81c1",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-18047",
      ":question/problem": "Let $a=\u27e85,9\u27e9.$ Find $|\\,a\\,|.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the formula, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(9)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+81} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{106}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186233595,
      ":question/difficulty": {
        ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/easy"
      },
      ":question/id": "26fce79e-92f6-594d-aec2-af45c6145c5c",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-18048",
      ":question/problem": "if $a=\u27e8-4,8\u27e9$, then  what is the magnitude of  $a?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
